WEBVTT

00:08.760 --> 00:11.760
The soil here has improved so much.

00:11.760 --> 00:14.510
Hey, Bel! Let's swap.

00:14.510 --> 00:15.380
Sure.

00:20.050 --> 00:22.720
She really likes these.

00:23.780 --> 00:26.130
I wonder when she's coming home.

00:26.130 --> 00:27.500
Excuse me!

00:30.810 --> 00:34.430
Hello. And who might you be?

00:34.430 --> 00:38.240
Do pardon the suddenness of my visit.

00:38.240 --> 00:42.420
Is this the residence of
Mr. Belgrieve the Red Ogre?

00:42.420 --> 00:46.210
Th-Th-The Red Ogre?

00:58.530 --> 01:06.750
<b>My Daughter Left the Nest and Returned an S-Rank Adventurer</b>

02:17.740 --> 02:22.990
<b>Episode 2 "Belgrieve the Red Ogre"</b>

02:20.830 --> 02:23.280
I'm Belgrieve.

02:23.280 --> 02:24.400
My!

02:25.480 --> 02:26.920
It's a pleasure to meet you.

02:26.920 --> 02:30.420
I am the second daughter of the 
Bordeaux family, Sasha Bordeaux.

02:31.570 --> 02:33.660
You're the count's daughter?

02:34.560 --> 02:37.690
I wasn't aware. Please forgive my rudeness.

02:37.690 --> 02:40.820
That's hardly necessary.
Please raise your head.

02:40.820 --> 02:43.680
The Bordeaux family owes 
Ms. Angeline a great debt.

02:43.680 --> 02:46.420
We're equally indebted to you as her father.

02:47.320 --> 02:50.320
You're indebted to Ange?

02:52.100 --> 02:53.020
Uh...

02:53.550 --> 02:54.820
I see it now.

02:54.820 --> 02:58.440
Your crimson hair certainly makes 
you worthy of the Red Ogre name.

02:58.910 --> 03:02.200
I think there's been a misunderstanding.

03:02.470 --> 03:03.390
What?!

03:03.390 --> 03:06.840
Do you mean to say there's another man
 named Belgrieve in this village?

03:06.840 --> 03:10.710
No, I'm the only Belgrieve here.

03:11.980 --> 03:19.460
Erm, I heard you were the father of
 Ms. Angeline the S-rank adventurer.

03:19.740 --> 03:22.590
Angeline is my daughter, yes.

03:23.020 --> 03:26.100
Then you <i>must</i> be Mr. Belgrieve the Red Ogre!

03:26.500 --> 03:28.450
The Red Ogre...

03:28.450 --> 03:33.070
Let's not speak out here. 
Would you like to come inside?

03:33.070 --> 03:35.370
Yes, thank you.

03:36.820 --> 03:39.500
I'm sorry I don't have 
anything better to offer.

03:39.500 --> 03:42.400
Oh, no. Don't worry about it.

03:42.400 --> 03:46.340
Anyway, Ms. Sasha, what can I do for you?

03:46.980 --> 03:47.860
That's right.

03:48.180 --> 03:53.380
Ms. Angeline rescued my 
youngest sister Seren from bandits

03:53.380 --> 03:57.410
and escorted her to our
 ailing father's bedside.

03:58.030 --> 04:01.430
How is Count Bordeaux doing?

04:02.340 --> 04:05.190
Because he was able to see 
Seren before his passing,

04:05.190 --> 04:07.410
he went to Lady Vienna without regret.

04:09.050 --> 04:12.950
I see. I'm sorry. I didn't know.

04:13.420 --> 04:15.390
My condolences for you loss.

04:15.390 --> 04:16.700
Thank you.

04:17.790 --> 04:21.810
Unfortunately, 
I did not meet Ms. Angeline myself,

04:22.190 --> 04:26.220
but she refused any kind of reward

04:26.220 --> 04:31.460
and said to give it to her father, 
Mr. Belgrieve, if we must.

04:32.810 --> 04:34.360
I see.

04:36.350 --> 04:37.930
I have one hundred gold coins here.

04:37.930 --> 04:39.210
What? A-A hundred?

04:39.760 --> 04:42.330
<i>I could live off a single coin for a year.</i>

04:42.710 --> 04:46.350
I'm sorry this is all I can provide for you.

04:46.350 --> 04:50.230
I can't accept this much.
Heaven would not stand for it.

04:50.230 --> 04:54.720
What are you talking about? 
Seren's life is priceless.

04:54.720 --> 04:59.810
It would be a disgrace to the 
Bordeaux family if you don't accept.

05:00.560 --> 05:02.140
Truly?

05:02.140 --> 05:02.910
Yes.

05:04.880 --> 05:06.580
Then I shall accept it.

05:07.460 --> 05:08.920
Thank you.

05:09.400 --> 05:11.740
<i>This reward is for Ange.</i>

05:11.740 --> 05:15.100
<i>I'll hold on to it until she comes home.</i>

05:15.740 --> 05:16.890
By the way...

05:17.450 --> 05:22.590
I heard you taught Ms. Angeline the sword
 and the basics of adventuring.

05:22.590 --> 05:25.030
When she was young, yes.

05:25.030 --> 05:27.460
I'm a novice adventurer as well.

05:27.460 --> 05:29.980
I'm still only Double A rank, though.

05:29.980 --> 05:32.330
<i>Double A at her age?</i>

05:32.330 --> 05:34.490
Forgive my impudence, but...

05:35.440 --> 05:38.850
Would you show me your swordplay 
by honoring me with a duel?

05:38.850 --> 05:39.720
What?

05:42.830 --> 05:46.360
I'm not sure I'm skilled enough 
to show anyone anything, but...

05:47.480 --> 05:48.860
You have my gratitude!

05:59.050 --> 06:01.120
Let us begin.

06:01.380 --> 06:04.030
<i>Her stance is beautiful. Interesting.</i>

06:24.680 --> 06:25.820
<i>What impact!</i>

06:30.260 --> 06:31.650
I lost...

06:33.040 --> 06:35.720
Thank you for the match.

06:36.970 --> 06:42.370
You must've been a famous 
adventurer in your day.

06:42.370 --> 06:45.640
I lost a leg when I was just getting started.

06:45.640 --> 06:50.340
I retired soon after, and I've been 
hiding out in Turnera ever since.

06:50.340 --> 06:52.870
I was only ever rank E.

06:52.870 --> 06:55.250
Wh-What? E?

06:57.940 --> 06:59.770
I'm impressed!

06:59.770 --> 07:01.030
What?

07:01.030 --> 07:04.640
Despite your wooden leg,
you've achieved such strength!

07:04.640 --> 07:08.070
I cannot begin to imagine
how hard you've trained!

07:08.070 --> 07:12.530
Not only that, but you protect Turnera 
rather than seeking a name for yourself.

07:12.960 --> 07:15.040
E-Er, Lady Sasha?

07:15.040 --> 07:19.550
On top of that, you raised 
an S-rank adventurer!

07:19.550 --> 07:21.380
Instead of pursuing fame and glory,

07:21.380 --> 07:26.510
you've dedicated yourself to guiding 
the next generation and this small village.

07:26.510 --> 07:28.610
You've shown me the light!

07:29.050 --> 07:31.540
Actually, uh...

07:31.850 --> 07:35.810
If I may be so bold, please allow me
 to call you my mentor as well.

07:36.070 --> 07:37.940
Hold on, Lady Sasha...

07:38.320 --> 07:41.560
Farewell now, Master! Until we meet again!

07:43.040 --> 07:43.840
Huh?

07:49.340 --> 07:52.390
<i>Was that a dream?</i>

07:56.290 --> 07:58.570
What? No jobs?

07:58.570 --> 08:01.820
There are no S-rank jobs available.

08:01.820 --> 08:04.080
Then can I take a month off?

08:04.080 --> 08:07.750
I-I'm afraid we can't do that.

08:07.750 --> 08:10.400
Monsters have been more active recently.

08:10.400 --> 08:12.840
There's no telling what may happen.

08:21.290 --> 08:24.170
You look super miserable.

08:24.170 --> 08:27.090
I don't need these tiny little breaks.

08:27.090 --> 08:30.100
Now, now.
You should appreciate your days off.

08:30.370 --> 08:36.390
It's not a real vacation unless I can go back
to Turnera for quality time with my father.

08:36.390 --> 08:38.790
You need someone to spoil you?

08:39.210 --> 08:44.360
There, there. Good girl. Who's a good girl?

08:46.750 --> 08:49.890
You couldn't hope to replace my father, Miri.

08:50.170 --> 08:54.540
The guild says there are no jobs,
but we're still at the mercy of monsters.

08:55.020 --> 09:00.900
Right? I feel like they
never used to attack the city.

09:01.840 --> 09:05.590
Why can't they just mind their own business 
somewhere far, far away from here?

09:05.930 --> 09:10.270
I've heard rumors that the demon kings
 may be returning. I wonder if that's it.

09:10.270 --> 09:15.870
That's hard to believe, but it is true that 
monsters are becoming more active.

09:16.220 --> 09:19.490
What's this about the demon kings?
Aren't there supposed to be a bunch?

09:19.490 --> 09:23.640
Yeah, the 72 demon kings of Solomon.

09:23.640 --> 09:26.110
If the legends are to be believed, that is.

09:26.110 --> 09:29.510
They were made by
Solomon the Great Wizard, right?

09:29.510 --> 09:30.380
Yup.

09:30.910 --> 09:35.120
He was a master of all 
kinds of magic and alchemy.

09:35.120 --> 09:38.820
He made a wide variety of
 spells and handy tools.

09:38.820 --> 09:43.080
But his incredible prowess 
drove him to hunger for power,

09:43.080 --> 09:46.850
and he created immortal constructs 
known as homunculi.

09:47.410 --> 09:50.940
He used them to conquer the land,

09:50.940 --> 09:54.140
but later in life, he lost his mind 
and control of his magic,

09:54.140 --> 09:56.610
eventually vanishing beyond 
the reaches of space-time.

09:57.120 --> 10:01.600
Without a master, the homunculi 
he left behind went on a rampage.

10:01.600 --> 10:03.820
They destroyed many a nation.

10:04.610 --> 10:07.750
Until at last, a hero blessed with
 Goddess Vienna's protection

10:07.750 --> 10:12.390
traveled the land to subdue the homunculi,
 bringing an end to the turmoil.

10:13.560 --> 10:17.500
They say those homunculi are the demon kings,
 but since it's all legend,

10:17.500 --> 10:19.710
no one knows for certain.

10:19.990 --> 10:21.570
Now that I think about it,

10:21.570 --> 10:25.980
there's a shady group that's been trying 
to bring back the demon kings recently.

10:25.980 --> 10:29.950
If the demon kings return, then it'll 
be even harder to get time off.

10:31.260 --> 10:34.440
I bet you'd be able to beat a demon king.

10:34.440 --> 10:36.670
Of course I could.

10:36.670 --> 10:39.690
I'm the daughter of Belgrieve the Red Ogre.

10:39.990 --> 10:42.530
I believe it, which is all the scarier.

10:44.060 --> 10:45.350
Ms. Angeline!

10:46.740 --> 10:48.720
A wyvern has been spotted.

10:48.720 --> 10:50.460
Could I ask you to handle it?

11:06.220 --> 11:07.290
Chief.

11:08.200 --> 11:09.450
Hey, Bel.

11:09.450 --> 11:11.250
Need help with anything?

11:11.250 --> 11:12.750
Can't say we do.

11:12.750 --> 11:15.810
The young'll never learn 
unless we make them do it.

11:15.810 --> 11:17.360
Heya, Bel!

11:18.010 --> 11:19.310
Hey, Kerry.

11:19.310 --> 11:21.480
Is Angeline coming home yet?

11:21.480 --> 11:23.450
Not yet, it seems.

11:23.450 --> 11:24.570
I see.

11:25.970 --> 11:28.400
I hear a bunch of urgent jobs came in.

11:28.400 --> 11:29.720
Um, excuse me.

11:30.710 --> 11:34.450
Are you Mr. Belgrieve the Red Ogre?

11:35.150 --> 11:40.340
This again? I am Belgrieve, yes.

11:40.340 --> 11:42.010
I knew it!

11:42.010 --> 11:44.140
You were talking about Ms. Angeline,

11:44.140 --> 11:47.220
and you have such magnificent red hair!

11:47.220 --> 11:49.240
That's, uh, right.

11:49.240 --> 11:52.800
Your daughter was actually
 my escort the other day.

11:52.800 --> 11:55.020
Oh, you don't say?

11:55.020 --> 11:58.980
While on the road, she gallantly 
rescued some people from bandits.

11:58.980 --> 12:01.700
The Black-Haired Valkyrie 
lives up to her reputation!

12:01.700 --> 12:03.120
Wow.

12:03.120 --> 12:05.420
Ange sure is working hard.

12:05.420 --> 12:06.270
Yeah.

12:13.020 --> 12:16.160
That's the crest of House Bordeaux.

12:16.450 --> 12:18.240
The Bordeaux family, eh?

12:18.240 --> 12:20.470
I'm sorry if I gave you a start.

12:21.310 --> 12:24.410
You see, I'm here looking for someone.

12:24.740 --> 12:27.080
I'm Hoffman, the chief of this village.

12:27.510 --> 12:31.920
You appear to be a member 
of the Bordeaux family.

12:31.920 --> 12:33.810
I should introduce myself.

12:33.810 --> 12:37.010
My name is Helvetica Bordeaux.

12:37.010 --> 12:39.460
As my father passed away recently,

12:39.460 --> 12:42.200
I am now Countess Bordeaux.

12:42.510 --> 12:45.310
So that's the famous Lady Helvetica.

12:45.310 --> 12:46.740
She's famous?

12:46.740 --> 12:49.960
Yeah. She's a charismatic warrior and scholar.

12:49.960 --> 12:51.530
Rather than taking a husband,

12:51.530 --> 12:54.410
she was named her father's heir 
and tasked with ruling his lands.

12:55.980 --> 12:58.080
I had no idea you were the countess.

12:58.080 --> 13:02.500
Please rise. I don't enjoy 
brandishing my authority.

13:02.500 --> 13:05.770
We are honored to have you here,

13:05.770 --> 13:09.560
but we harbor no criminals
or fugitives in this village.

13:09.560 --> 13:13.270
Worry not. I did not come
 in pursuit of any criminal.

13:13.270 --> 13:18.950
I am here to meet Mr. Belgrieve the Red Ogre.

13:18.950 --> 13:22.970
What? Belgrieve... the Red Ogre?

13:27.010 --> 13:28.710
You are Mr. Belgrieve, are you not?

13:28.710 --> 13:31.190
Y-Yes, I am.

13:31.190 --> 13:35.660
I am grateful your daughter 
rescued my younger sister.

13:35.660 --> 13:38.500
U-Uh, you're welcome.

13:40.050 --> 13:42.720
I see you're rather well-trained.

13:42.720 --> 13:46.320
And I've heard you're 
impressive with a sword.

13:46.320 --> 13:50.000
Oh, uh... thank you.

13:50.000 --> 13:53.420
I actually came today 
because I have a request.

13:55.010 --> 13:57.510
Allow me to be direct.

13:57.810 --> 14:02.020
Mr. Belgrieve, I would like you 
to serve the Bordeaux family.

14:03.070 --> 14:04.020
What?

14:05.760 --> 14:08.810
B-Bel? Serve the Bordeaux family?

14:14.540 --> 14:15.500
Now then...

14:15.500 --> 14:16.890
I'm sorry.

14:17.570 --> 14:21.190
I have no intention of leaving Turnera.

14:21.190 --> 14:24.800
I'm already 42, and I'm only getting weaker.

14:24.800 --> 14:27.410
I doubt I'd be of any use to you as I am.

14:27.410 --> 14:29.210
Whatever do you mean?

14:29.500 --> 14:33.980
I heard from Sasha that 
you defeated her with ease.

14:34.510 --> 14:37.720
We would love to employ such strength.

14:37.960 --> 14:41.990
Maybe it's because I used to be an adventurer,
 but I'm not cut out to serve a liege.

14:41.990 --> 14:43.910
Won't you please make an exception?

14:43.910 --> 14:44.870
I'm afraid not.

14:44.870 --> 14:46.860
We'd be willing to pay you anything.

14:46.860 --> 14:48.510
I simply cannot.

14:48.510 --> 14:52.540
I insist, please come to me.

14:52.540 --> 14:54.120
I'm very sorry.

14:55.860 --> 15:00.620
I see. You're as stubborn as you are strong.

15:01.640 --> 15:04.120
I was born that way, too.

15:04.910 --> 15:07.640
Then you leave me no choice.

15:07.640 --> 15:09.820
Come, everyone.

15:09.820 --> 15:10.830
Yes, milady!

15:10.830 --> 15:14.890
We'll take him back by force.

15:15.290 --> 15:16.380
What?

15:22.060 --> 15:25.800
I'll do whatever it takes to
 make you serve my family.

15:29.810 --> 15:34.860
<i>She may be the countess,
yet she's still but a young girl inside.</i>

15:34.860 --> 15:37.460
<i>The responsibility must 
be making her desperate.</i>

15:37.460 --> 15:42.150
So be it. I shall take on 
your men until you relent.

15:51.410 --> 15:54.460
Hey, what's gotten into all of you?

15:54.460 --> 15:56.570
He's just one man.

15:56.570 --> 15:58.140
B-But...

15:58.140 --> 15:59.640
He's utterly unassailable!

16:04.890 --> 16:07.690
I admit you've thoroughly bested me.

16:07.690 --> 16:09.650
Are we on the same page now?

16:10.510 --> 16:11.900
Since it's come to this...

16:13.430 --> 16:17.060
I have no choice but to become yours instead!

16:17.060 --> 16:18.020
What?

16:18.020 --> 16:19.760
Bel's marrying up?

16:19.760 --> 16:22.780
This autumn festival's gonna be a wedding!

16:22.780 --> 16:26.810
Though you may find me lacking, 
I hope you'll have me.

16:26.810 --> 16:27.820
But, uh...

16:27.820 --> 16:29.050
Sister!

16:30.820 --> 16:33.800
What did you come here to do?

16:34.200 --> 16:37.300
Why, I came to persuade
Mr. Belgrieve to join us.

16:37.300 --> 16:40.090
You tried to cart him off by force, 
didn't you?

16:41.940 --> 16:43.870
Lock her in the carriage!

16:43.870 --> 16:44.470
Yes, milady!

16:47.080 --> 16:49.350
I'm sorry for the trouble.

16:49.350 --> 16:51.160
You're Mr. Belgrieve, aren't you?

16:51.640 --> 16:53.020
I-I am.

16:53.020 --> 16:54.960
My name is Seren Bordeaux.

16:54.960 --> 17:00.960
Ms. Angeline saved my life and took me
 to see my father on his deathbed.

17:00.960 --> 17:03.000
I'd like to express my gratitude.

17:03.310 --> 17:06.000
Please forgive my sister's rude display.

17:06.000 --> 17:10.000
It's fine. I'm not offended.

17:10.240 --> 17:14.520
Thank you. Normally, 
she's perfectly respectable,

17:14.520 --> 17:18.750
but when she hears of exceptional 
talent, she can't help herself.

17:20.780 --> 17:23.980
Let me out. I promise I won't do it again.

17:23.510 --> 17:27.080
No! I'm not letting you out
 until we get home!

17:28.470 --> 17:32.070
Come, everyone. Let's not bother 
these folks any longer. We're off.

17:32.920 --> 17:37.290
But if you leave now,
 it'll be dark before you get far.

17:37.290 --> 17:39.020
This is how it must be.

17:39.020 --> 17:41.040
We cannot impose on you, after all.

17:41.040 --> 17:43.280
The autumn festival is tonight.

17:43.280 --> 17:45.780
Why don't you stick around?

17:46.810 --> 17:48.530
What? But...

17:48.790 --> 17:52.910
We'd be honored to have the
 countess's family join us.

17:52.910 --> 17:54.180
Right, Chief?

17:54.180 --> 17:57.660
Sure enough! Our shabby little village
 would love to have you.

17:57.660 --> 18:00.550
In that case, if you insist.

18:00.550 --> 18:03.350
I do, but I have one condition.

18:04.030 --> 18:06.930
Please let Lady Helvetica
 out of the carriage.

18:11.950 --> 18:14.930
If you say so, Mr. Belgrieve.

18:17.360 --> 18:20.580
Mr. Belgrieve, you have my deepest gratitude!

18:22.170 --> 18:23.830
It's not that big a deal.

18:23.830 --> 18:27.470
How merciful! I simply must have you
 for the Bordeaux family.

18:27.470 --> 18:28.690
Sister!

18:28.690 --> 18:30.700
I-I was merely kidding.

18:32.160 --> 18:33.390
Hey, hey!

18:33.720 --> 18:36.260
Let's have some cowberries.

18:36.260 --> 18:38.820
Come with us, scary lady.

18:39.500 --> 18:40.470
Scary?

18:41.800 --> 18:44.340
She's really a very sweet girl.

18:49.940 --> 18:52.360
Ange, over here!

18:53.080 --> 18:55.860
Did you two already defeat the monsters?

18:56.170 --> 18:59.880
Yeah, Miri's area-of-effect spells
 made quick work of them.

19:00.970 --> 19:05.880
By the way, does the guild have any idea 
why so many monsters are cropping up?

19:05.880 --> 19:07.980
Not at all.

19:07.980 --> 19:13.820
The adventurers dispatched to determine 
why they're appearing so quickly

19:13.820 --> 19:16.540
are also overwhelmed
just handling their numbers.

19:16.540 --> 19:21.700
Lots of adventurers are leaving Orphen 
because they hate being so busy.

19:21.700 --> 19:23.920
We're going to be short-handed soon.

19:23.920 --> 19:28.500
I told the guild master to call in
retired adventurers, too.

19:28.500 --> 19:29.950
Thank you for waiting.

19:29.950 --> 19:31.020
Thanks.

19:31.680 --> 19:33.930
Wait, retired adventurers...

19:34.820 --> 19:36.810
What is it, Ange?

19:37.050 --> 19:39.920
I just had an incredible idea.

19:39.920 --> 19:44.700
I should ask my dad to come to 
Orphen and resume adventuring.

19:44.700 --> 19:46.140
Come to think of it,

19:46.140 --> 19:49.450
didn't you say he's so strong 
you've never landed a blow on him?

19:49.450 --> 19:53.290
It'd solve the adventurer shortage, 
<i>and</i> you'd get to see your dad.

19:53.290 --> 19:54.730
Two birds with one stone!

19:54.730 --> 19:59.580
Damn, why didn't I think of that sooner? 
I'm such a dummy!

20:03.870 --> 20:08.560
But I feel like my dad and 
Turnera are inseparable...

20:12.960 --> 20:14.860
I want to go home...

20:16.320 --> 20:17.470
Ms. Angeline?

20:19.110 --> 20:20.720
Oh, you're that merchant.

20:20.720 --> 20:22.850
Thank you for your help before.

20:23.180 --> 20:24.770
You know each other?

20:24.770 --> 20:27.230
Yes, I escorted her for a job.

20:27.230 --> 20:31.480
By the way, I visited 
Turnera during the autumn festival.

20:31.480 --> 20:32.960
I met your father there.

20:33.880 --> 20:35.600
Is he doing well?!

20:35.600 --> 20:37.350
What'd you do? What'd you talk about?

20:39.690 --> 20:42.300
Uh, he was doing great.

20:42.300 --> 20:46.380
He readily handled a group of the 
Bordeaux family's bodyguards.

20:46.660 --> 20:49.140
He did what? Why?

20:49.680 --> 20:52.880
Lady Helvetica, the new countess,
came to see him...

20:54.100 --> 20:58.980
How dare she try to take my dad from me!

20:58.980 --> 21:01.650
She may be Seren's sister, 
but she won't get away with this!

21:01.650 --> 21:06.040
Now, now. The whole thing was called off.

21:06.040 --> 21:09.840
Of course. I knew my dad
could handle it. He's the coolest.

21:10.320 --> 21:11.790
I bet he was awesome!

21:11.790 --> 21:14.660
Yes. Honestly, I was surprised.

21:14.660 --> 21:17.140
He really lives up to the name "Red Ogre."

21:19.270 --> 21:21.570
You've got a good eye.

21:21.570 --> 21:23.570
Let me treat you today.

21:23.570 --> 21:26.690
We must discuss my dad's 
charms at great length.

21:26.690 --> 21:27.790
Um...

21:28.820 --> 21:30.920
What? For real?

21:31.170 --> 21:34.380
It's settled! I'm in such a good mood,
I'll treat you guys, too!

21:34.380 --> 21:35.980
Heck yeah!

21:35.980 --> 21:40.580
U-Um, I appreciate it, but I have business 
negotiations early tomorrow morning.

21:40.830 --> 21:42.160
Don't fight it.

21:42.160 --> 21:45.810
Once Ange starts talking about
 the Red Ogre, you can't stop her.

21:56.010 --> 21:57.680
Master...

21:59.140 --> 22:00.530
I'm so lonely...

22:01.980 --> 22:03.540
Master...

23:35.060 --> 23:40.010
<b>Next Time</b>

23:35.060 --> 23:40.010
<b>"Welcome Home, Angeline"</b>
